@page "/visible-columns"
@using NxGrid.Demo.Shared.Data

<PageTitle>Visible Columns — NxGrid</PageTitle>

<h1>Visible Columns</h1>
<p class="doc-intro">
    <code>Visible</code> is a programmer-controlled gate that removes a column entirely from the
    grid and from the column chooser. Unlike <code>Hidden</code>, it cannot be changed by the user
    and is never saved to localStorage. The intended use is authorization-based column visibility —
    show a column only to users with the appropriate role.
</p>

<div class="doc-section">
    <h2>Try it</h2>
    <p class="doc-note">
        The <strong>Salary</strong> column is only visible when "Manager" is checked. When unchecked
        the column does not exist in the grid — it is not in the column chooser and cannot be shown
        by the user. Toggle the checkbox to simulate a role change.
    </p>
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:10px">
        <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;cursor:pointer;font-weight:500">
            <input type="checkbox" @bind="isManager" style="width:16px;height:16px" />
            I am a manager — show salary data
        </label>
    </div>
    <NxGrid T="Person" Data="@rows" Style="height:320px" RowGutter="NxGridRowGutter.Numbers"
            HasColumnMenu="true" Cursor="@NxGridCursor.Cell">
        <NxGridColumn Display="@(x => x.FirstName + " " + x.LastName)" Title="Name" Width="180" />
        <NxGridColumn Property="@(x => x.Department)" Width="140" />
        <NxGridColumn Property="@(x => x.Age)"        Width="80"  Alignment="NxGridColumnAlignment.Right" />
        <NxGridColumn Property="@(x => x.Salary)"     Width="120" Visible="@isManager"
                      Display="@(x => x.Salary.ToString("C0"))"
                      Alignment="NxGridColumnAlignment.Right" />
    </NxGrid>
    <pre class="doc-code" style="margin-top:12px">@basicCode</pre>
</div>

<div class="doc-section">
    <h2>Visible vs Hidden</h2>
    <p class="doc-note">
        <code>Visible="false"</code> and <code>Hidden="true"</code> both exclude a column from
        rendering, but they serve different purposes:
    </p>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>
            <code>Visible="false"</code> — the column does not exist for the current user.
            It is absent from the column chooser. No user action can reveal it.
            Useful when the column's existence should be conditional on authorization.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>Hidden="true"</code> — the column is collapsed by default but the user
            can show it via <strong>Manage columns…</strong> in the column menu. Use this
            when the column is simply not displayed initially but is available on request.
        </li>
        <li>
            <code>Hidden="true" Hideable="false"</code> — permanently hidden from rendering
            but still participates in sort and filter. Use this to filter or sort by a field
            without showing it as a column.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <pre class="doc-code">@vsHiddenCode</pre>
</div>

@code {
    List<Person> rows = SampleData.People.ToList();
    bool isManager = false;

    string basicCode    = DemoCodeSamples.VisibleBasic;
    string vsHiddenCode = DemoCodeSamples.VisibleVsHidden;
}
